<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Temne people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Temne are a West African people of northern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a>, one of the country's two largest ethnic groups alongside the Mende. They speak a Mel language, and before colonial rule they were organised in chiefdoms such as Koya on the Sierra Leone estuary, whose rulers granted the land on which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a> was founded. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> spread among them from the 18th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/temne-people.jpg" alt="Temne people" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: gbaku · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TemneChildren.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
